WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.408
A definition of done.

2
00:00:01.688 --> 00:00:05.891
Write the definition of done before you build, so you are testing against something.

3
00:00:06.171 --> 00:00:09.712
Here is a starting point for the project; tighten it as you learn.

4
00:00:09.992 --> 00:00:17.181
The pipeline runs end to end on a set of realistic transcripts, including messy ones, with no unhandled errors.

5
00:00:17.461 --> 00:00:22.965
Every item shown to the reviewer has an evidence quote that appears verbatim in the transcript.

6
00:00:23.245 --> 00:00:31.864
Owners resolve to directory entries or are explicitly unassigned, never guessed; dates resolve by documented rules or are flagged.

7
00:00:32.144 --> 00:00:40.144
Nothing is written to the tracker without approval, writes are idempotent, and the model has no tool that can send data outside the system.

8
00:00:40.424 --> 00:00:47.528
On your labeled set, recall and precision meet bars you chose in advance, and you report them with the size of the set.

9
00:00:47.808 --> 00:00:51.669
Cost per meeting is measured from real usage, not estimated.

10
00:00:51.949 --> 00:00:54.659
Every run produces the log described above.

11
00:00:54.939 --> 00:00:58.672
And you can explain, for each model choice, what evidence led to it.
